# acidcandy — the FX HUB reachability + VOWEL device regression seed (2026-07-28).
#
# This exists because the hub's first cut hid the knob pages behind a HOLD on a chip and they were
# promptly unfindable (the same "hidden meta-mode" that killed this cart's old 4-way pad tool). The
# fix was: a plain TAP opens the page. That is a UI-reachability claim, so it gets a deterministic
# seed rather than a promise — every step below is one plain tap, no gestures.
#
# The route, in phone (single-face) layout on the 160x100 canvas:
#   1. the MST cartridge in the nav strip (5th tab)
#   2. the FX soft-key (left column, 5th key) -> the chip menu
#   3. ONE tap on the VOWEL chip        -> must land on the VOWEL knob page
#   4. the ON key (page header, right)  -> arms the master formant
#   5. drag the MIX knob up             -> must reach the audio
#
# Verified (400 frames, script /dev/null-style fixed timestep, so these are reproducible):
#   through step 3 only  -> sha 39150390ac4a, byte-identical to the everything-off baseline
#                           (i.e. navigating the UI is audibly inert, as it must be)
#   + step 4 (ON)        -> sha 9439f2b966a9, rms -22.93 dBFS
#   + step 5 (MIX drag)  -> sha f79fa4d7e9fa, rms -21.96 dBFS, knob readout 99
# rms RISING as MIX rises is correct, not a bug: the formant bandpasses have resonant gain (the
# ab-render sweep shows peak -6.6 dBFS at mix 0.7 climbing to -4.2 at 1.0).
#
#   node tools/play.js acidcandy script tools/clips/acidcandy/05-fx-hub-vowel.script \
#        --headless --frames 400 --wav /tmp/vow.wav
#   node tools/play.js acidcandy script tools/clips/acidcandy/05-fx-hub-vowel.script \
#        --headless --frames 200 --dump /tmp/vowdump      # eyeball the page at ~frame 165
#
# If a tap lands somewhere unexpected after a layout change, THAT is the signal — the coordinates are
# hand-measured against the phone face, so this seed doubles as a layout tripwire.
click 20 130 8      # nav strip: focus the MST cartridge
click 45 9 71       # left soft-key column: FX -> the device chip menu
click 70 40 58      # ONE tap on the VOWEL chip -> its knob page (no hold needed)
click 95 115 49     # the page's ON key -> arm the master formant
drag 120 113 61 170 113 44   # MIX knob: press at (113,61), glide up to y44, release at frame 170
